<title>NORWAY: Saga takeover of Santa Fe completed.</title>
<headline>Saga takeover of Santa Fe completed.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saga Petroleum, Norway's largest independent oil company, said on Friday British authorities had formally approved of its acquisition of North Sea explorer Santa Fe Exploration.</p>
<p>&quot;Saga Petroleum confirms that British authorities have cleared the transfer of oil licenses and that the purchase of shares in KP North Sea Holdings ltd (Santa Fe) is completed,&quot; the Oslo Bourse said in a brief statement.</p>
<p>Saga on December 4 confirmed the widely known $1.23 billion take-over of Santa Fe in a deal with state-owned Kuwait Petroleum Corp.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
